``as_string()`` no longer renders an unterminated f-string when the body ends
with the character of the triple-quoted delimiter it picked. A trailing ``"``
right before the closing delimiter was read as four quotes in a row, so
``f'{"b"}a"'`` came out as ``f"""...a""""`` and neither ``parse()`` nor
``brain_dataclasses`` / ``brain_namedtuple_enum`` could use the result.

Refs #3235
